  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "In each of the following, $f(x)$ was transformed a certain way for it to become $g(x)$. Describe the transformation.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q3a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$, $g(x)=\\sqrt{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Translate 1 unit to the left.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=\\sqrt{x+1}\\\\g(x)&=f(x+1)\\end{align*}$$\n\nAdding 1 to the input translates the graph 1 unit to the left.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$, $g(x)=\\sqrt{x}+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Translate 2 units up.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=\\sqrt{x}+2\\\\g(x)&=f(x)+2\\end{align*}$$\n\nAdding 2 to the output translates the graph 2 units up.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\ln(x+1)$, $g(x)=\\ln(2x+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Squash horizontally by a factor of 2.\n\nEach $x$-coordinate is halved.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=\\ln(2x+1)\\\\g(x)&=f(2x)\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe old input $u$ now occurs at $x=\\frac u2$. The graph is squashed horizontally by a factor of 2.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{2}{x-1}$, $g(x)=\\frac{1}{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Squash vertically by a factor of 2.\n\nEach $y$-coordinate is halved.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=\\frac{1}{x-1}\\\\g(x)&=\\frac12\\cdot\\frac{2}{x-1}\\\\g(x)&=\\frac12 f(x)\\end{align*}$$\n\nHalving the output squashes the graph vertically by a factor of 2.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=e^x+1$, $g(x)=e^x-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Translate 3 units down.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=e^x-2\\\\g(x)&=(e^x+1)-3\\\\g(x)&=f(x)-3\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubtracting 3 from the output translates the graph 3 units down.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 9
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=(x+1)^2$, $g(x)=(x-3)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Translate 4 units to the right.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=(x-3)^2\\\\g(x)&=((x-4)+1)^2\\\\g(x)&=f(x-4)\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubtracting 4 from the input translates the graph 4 units to the right.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 9
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=4x^2-1$, $g(x)=x^2-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Stretch horizontally by a factor of 2.\n\nEach $x$-coordinate is doubled.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=x^2-1\\\\g(x)&=4\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2-1\\\\g(x)&=f\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe old input $u$ now occurs at $x=2u$. The graph is stretched horizontally by a factor of 2.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      }
    ]
  },
